@prefix conf: <https://hexplain.io/ns/conf#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

conf:ConstraintShape skos:definition "Applies to instances of conf:Constraint; subjects using conf:assertion, conf:message, conf:scope; objects of conf:findingConstraint. A Constraint needs exactly one non-empty conf:assertion HEL expression. A Constraint needs exactly one non-empty conf:message finding template. A Constraint must cite at least one req:Requirement; an unattributed rule cannot be reported. A Constraint needs exactly one conf:scope IRI naming the bddo:Struct or bddo:Field it applies to. A Constraint states at most one conf:severity: sh:Violation, sh:Warning or sh:Info (absent means sh:Violation)."@en .
conf:RangeDatatypeShape skos:definition "Applies to subjects using conf:assertion, conf:fileVersion, conf:findingMessage, conf:message, conf:truncated, conf:truncationReason, conf:versionScopingApplied. conf:assertion takes a HEL expression, an xsd:string or bddo:HelExpression literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). conf:fileVersion takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). conf:findingMessage takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). conf:message takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). conf:truncated takes an xsd:boolean literal (rdfs:range xsd:boolean). conf:truncationReason takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). conf:versionScopingApplied takes an xsd:boolean literal (rdfs:range xsd:boolean)."@en .
conf:_prefixes rdfs:label "prefixes"@en ;
    skos:definition "Namespace prefix declarations reused by SHACL SPARQL constraints and rules. This is validation infrastructure, not a property of parsed data."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/conf/shapes> skos:scopeNote "Load with the conf vocabulary to validate conformance profiles (constraints, parse attributions) and run reports (runs, outcomes, findings). A report validates on its own because it carries copies of the requirements, constraints and attributions it cites."@en .
